# Readline configuration for the shell the E2E daemon spawns.
#
# Bracketed paste is off. With it on — the default since bash 5.1 — a pasted
# block is inserted into the line buffer as literal text and the newlines inside
# it do not submit anything, so every test that pastes a command and waits for
# its marker hangs until the timeout. The suite pastes deliberately: chunked
# paste is how it proves input transport preserves ordering across chunk
# boundaries, and that only means anything if the pasted commands actually run.
#
# This is not a workaround for the shell pin; it restores the behaviour the pin
# is meant to reproduce. `/bin/sh` on macOS is bash 3.2, which predates
# bracketed paste entirely, so the tests were written against a shell that
# executes pasted newlines.
set enable-bracketed-paste off
